    <string name="spoof_magisk_title">Magisk Module Generator</string>
    <string name="spoof_magisk_building">Building ZIP…</string>
    <string name="spoof_magisk_desc">Flashable ZIP of your first profile. Carries the model identity only — kept minimal so a flash cannot boot-loop the device. Applies device-wide, so Safe Mode exclusions do not apply. After a reboot the module reports which properties actually landed, and its action button opens a WebUI. This app\'s own APK rides along, so the module can restore the app after it is gone.</string>
    <string name="spoof_root_manager_title">Open Root Manager</string>
    <string name="spoof_root_manager_desc">Access Magisk/KernelSU/APatch.</string>
    <string name="spoof_root_manager_need">Needs root access.</string>
    <!-- Method exclusivity: Xposed hooks vs generated Catsmoker module -->
    <string name="spoof_method_magisk_installed">Catsmoker module installed</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_magisk_installed_sub">Installed and enabled in your root manager; it applies identity at boot.</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_magisk_disabled">Catsmoker module disabled</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_magisk_disabled_sub">Installed but disabled in your root manager, so it changes nothing.</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_magisk_absent">No module installed</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_magisk_absent_sub">No separately installed Catsmoker module was found on this device.</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_magisk_unknown">Module state unknown (needs root to check)</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_magisk_unknown_sub">Grant root to check whether a separately installed Catsmoker module exists.</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_conflict_title">Two spoofing methods at once</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_conflict_body">The Catsmoker module is installed and Vector has our integration enabled. Both rewrite device identity, so Catsmoker disables only its own Vector integration through Vector\'s CLI and then verifies the manager row. Games already running keep the old injection until they restart.</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_conflict_failed">The Vector manager still reports our integration enabled. Nothing else was changed.</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_conflict_retry">RETRY DISABLE</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_conflict_disabled">Catsmoker module installed — Vector integration disabled and verified.</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_conflict_disable_failed">Could not verify the Vector integration was disabled. Open Vector and disable Catsmoker\'s module there, then refresh.</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_confirm_assign_title">Assign with Catsmoker module installed?</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_confirm_assign_body">The separately installed Catsmoker module applies identity device-wide. Assigning an Xposed profile too means two methods rewrite identity. Catsmoker will disable its Vector integration after the module is installed and verified; continue?</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_confirm_generate_title">Generate while Xposed is in use?</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_confirm_generate_body">Xposed profiles are assigned or the module is loaded. The generated module only takes effect after you flash it and reboot; once it is installed, Catsmoker will disable only its own Vector integration so the two never stay active together. Continue?</string>
    <string name="spoof_method_use_anyway">Use anyway</string>
